---8<--- [start:description]

`pixi lock --check` implies `--dry-run`: it reports the changes that would be made
without creating or modifying `pixi.lock` or installing environments. It exits
with a non-zero code if the lock file is missing or out of date.

--8<-- [end:description]

---8<--- [start:example]

## Examples

```shell
pixi lock
pixi lock --manifest-path ~/myworkspace/pixi.toml
pixi lock --json
pixi lock --check
```

--8<-- [end:example]
